subsections.description:
This is the default and the fastest path. Call the `create_tool` method with a name, a one-line description, the methods it exposes (each with parameters), and a `code` string exporting a `handlers` object. The keys of `handlers` ARE the method names — name them well; you do not restate them anywhere. The backend derives each method's schema from the parameters, so `code` is JUST the handlers.

```js
// code:
export const handlers = {
  celsius_to_fahrenheit: async ({ celsius }) => ({ fahrenheit: celsius * 9/5 + 32 }),
  fahrenheit_to_celsius: async ({ fahrenheit }) => ({ celsius: (fahrenheit - 32) * 5/9 }),
};
```

Each handler receives the parsed `args` and returns any JSON value. The tool is global the moment it is created; assign it to an agent before it can be called. Do not put an `id` in the definition — it is derived from the name.
